<!--Post: 2884--><!--Time: 1104228469-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2884"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 2:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This may be a really stupid question on my part, but how do you watch somebody&#39;s house without being noticed? <BR> <BR>From what I&#39;ve been able to tell from reading the history, these murders all took place in regular neighborhoods as opposed to out in the country or in densely populated, high traffic areas &#40;like NYC, for instance&#41;.  What I mean by &#34;regular neighborhoods&#34; is just that.  Just some houses on a street with your typical neighborhood traffic, i.e., people taking children to school, going to work and coming home from work at various hours, visitors coming and going, people walking their dogs, people taking a stroll, people doing yard work or working on their homes, etc.  I&#39;m from Tulsa and almost every neighborhood there would fit this description, so I can&#39;t imagine that Wichita would be any different. <BR> <BR>I may be nosier than the average person, I don&#39;t know.  I only know that there is no way someone could sit in a car and watch a house in a &#34;regular neighborhood&#34; without being noticed by somebody.  From everything I&#39;ve read, it does seem to be a given that BTK must have watched his victims so he could ascertain what would be the best time for him to attack without being disturbed. <BR> <BR>I can only assume that BTK didn’t sit in a vehicle or stand around being an obvious stranger in order to watch the homes of his victims.  That makes no sense.  Even if he was around posing as a utility worker, park employee, etc., how could he hang around for long?  After a while, people are going to wonder why the dude from the electric company keeps coming back.   <BR> <BR>Trying to go with a BTK frame of mind here, the only way I can think of that I would watch my potential victims at home would be if I was someplace where nobody could see me, like inside another, nearby house.  I’m not saying I would break into a house to sit and watch, but I would be in some line of work that gave me good cause to be at another house, probably for several days in a row at least.  Maybe I would be a roofer or a landscaper?  Better yet, going with the theory in another thread that BTK may have had access to rental homes &#40;if the victims rented&#41;, I would be tending to rental houses in the neighborhood.  If BTK had a reason to be in another house nearby, especially if it was an empty house, he could sit on his butt all day in there and watch people.  Nobody would notice. <BR> <BR>The only other plausible theory I can come up with is that he didn’t watch his victims at all because he knew them well enough to know their schedules.  Or else, back to my question, how do you watch somebody without being noticed?  How would you all do it?  What would be the most ideal situation/line of work to do that? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2884-->
<!--Post: 2888--><!--Time: 1104236125-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2888"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 4:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very good question! very good thinking Jujuree! <BR> <BR>I think the version BTK beeing a real estate agent/salesman &#40;dont know if that is the correct term, I`m danish<IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> having access to empty houses/apartments. And that BTK FIRST chooses the empty house or apartment, maybe from housenumbers or other things that have special meanings to BTK, and then from his voyeur spot select his victims. <BR>Wonder if it has been checked if there were houses/apartments for sale, in som way, across the street of the victims? <BR> <BR>Just my humble shot on the question<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2888-->
<!--Post: 2890--><!--Time: 1104238097-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2890"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 4:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is/was there a bus line that ran down any of the streets? Taxis can sit anywhere usually also...just another thought!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2890-->
<!--Post: 2894--><!--Time: 1104242518-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2894"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 6:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The taxi theory is a good one, especially if there were any hotels nearby.  If a person had a line of sight from the front of a hotel, they could sit there for a long time watching a house.  I assume all he would be interested in seeing is when the person he&#39;s watching is home and if they get any visitors.   <BR> <BR>Also, I wonder if there are/were any tall buildings near the murder sites?  A person can see for quite a distance from a tall building.  The building wouldn&#39;t even have to be that tall.  The building&#39;s proximity to the homes would dictate how tall it would have to be in order to spy from a window there.  It could be an office building or a hotel, empty or not.  If BTK had his own office or found an abandoned building, he could use binoculars or a telescope and watch undisturbed and unnoticed. <BR> <BR>In that scenario, watching from a house or a nearby &#42;tall&#42; building might have been what stopped him.  If he lost the job/situation that allowed him access to whatever building&#40;s&#41; he used, then he wouldn&#39;t have been able to continue watching.  An abandoned building he used may have been torn down or become occupied or he might have lost his job as a realtor or property manager. <BR> <BR>BTK may not have been willing to continue his attacks with the element of suprise working against him.  Any other riskier form of surveillance may not have been acceptable to him, especially when compared to the security of what he had become accustomed to.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2894-->
<!--Post: 2895--><!--Time: 1104243076-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2895"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 6:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have held a long theory that he watched his victims from nearby wooded areas or parks. A theory that I believe was bolsted with the  recent communication found in a park. I think he might have spyed from neabry trees. I also give credence to the idea that he might work for the park service.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2895-->
<!--Post: 2896--><!--Time: 1104245758-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2896"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 6:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK watching from nearby wooded areas is very plausible, I think.  I have no idea what the landscape was like around the areas in question as far as wooded areas go, but that would probably have been the easiest way for BTK to watch someone without being seen.  As with my tall building theory, BTK could have been in wooded areas watching with the aid of binoculars or a telescope, so he wouldn&#39;t have had to be really close to his targets. <BR> <BR>I have problems with the park services theory.  Park maintenance workers are usually pretty busy.  Usually, they show up and mow, pick up litter or whatever else they&#39;re supposed to do and they&#39;re out of there.  I&#39;ve never observed park maintenance workers loitering around the way a person would need to if they were trying to watch a house.  I just don&#39;t see how they could work and adequately watch. <BR> <BR>I guess what it boils down to for me is I can&#39;t imagine BTK turning his attention away at all.  I think he was very focused on watching, if that is indeed what he did.  I think the watching was a part of his &#34;process,&#34; and he enjoyed every moment of it.  It would only take a moment for a neighbor to walk over to a target&#39;s home, knock and be invited in.  If BTK was mowing the park or pulling up weeds, he could easily miss that and there would be no visiting car at the house to alert him to it. <BR> <BR>The other problem I have with that is I can&#39;t imagine BTK being around in a uniformed capacity to watch, so that he could watch in the open.  No matter how he dressed when he killed, if someone saw him, they might recognize him as the park maintenance guy.  IOW, if he was out in the open in any capacity as he did his surveillance, he would be seen by the same people in the area who could potentially see him when he was going to or coming from an attack.  <BR> <BR>I just keep coming back to BTK watching while completely hidden, in a nearby building or, as you mentioned, in a wooded area.  I could be completely wrong, but I can&#39;t imagine BTK risking much in his planning stages.  Shoot!  For all I know he might have been one of those people going around neighborhoods painting the house addresses on the curbs!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2896-->
<!--Post: 2899--><!--Time: 1104251297-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2899"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 8:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He couldve also hidden in the dark/shadows in the back yard or beside the house for HOURS if needed.  You dont happen to live in that area do you jujuree?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2899-->
<!--Post: 2901--><!--Time: 1104252962-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2901"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 8:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another idea i&#39;ve had, was that in his older years <BR>BTK would be part or join his neighborhood watch comittee. This would allow him an excuse if you will to be out at night watching people.I believe this would be a very hard aspect of his past behavior to change. The watching aspect. I think he would still practice this without actually killing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2901-->
<!--Post: 2905--><!--Time: 1104255272-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2905"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 9:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Scbenson, I think that could be very true, that BTK is still watching people.  That definitely adds to the creep factor.  If he still watches, I wonder if it&#39;s because he&#39;s no longer physically capable of killing, due to age, illness or injury?  Or maybe he does it to test his resolve not to kill.  Though, based on his latest letters, he doesn&#39;t seem to have any remorse.  He still sounds pretty boastful to me.  Based on that, I don&#39;t see that he&#39;d try very hard not to kill if the urge hit him. <BR> <BR>And to Vdubguy, no, I&#39;m not from the Wichita area.  I&#39;ve never been there.  I&#39;m in Oklahoma.  If BTK&#39;s still lurking around, hiding behind bushes in the dark eating BLTs while watching people, then Oklahoma&#39;s probably a pretty good place to be! <BR> <BR>Back to seriousness again, it&#39;s this &#34;watching&#34; part that drives me nuts more than anything else.  I just can&#39;t get past that.  If he watched, I don&#39;t think he was seen at all and I don&#39;t think there are a whole lot of options on how one would do that.  You&#39;re either going to be inside a structure or in a wooded area.  Are there any other options that would keep one totally unnoticed in a residential area?  An unfamiliar vehicle with someone sitting inside of it for hours on end would attract attention.  If he didn&#39;t watch, he either had to have known the victims &#40;or he knew them through a third party&#41; or his attacks were purely spur of the moment, a scenario I find unlikely.  The execution of his crimes &#40;literally&#41; seem too well planned. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2905-->
<!--Post: 2910--><!--Time: 1104261544-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2910"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 11:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->jujuree <BR>Ive been thorouhg Wichita a bunch...and used to live in OKC and Edmond OK... <BR>I stick with the idea that he was lurking in the dark for a good part of the night...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2910-->
<!--Post: 2913--><!--Time: 1104266695-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2913"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 12:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->All of this talk about hiding and watching implies that everything always went as he expected.  Yet, &#42;IF&#42; Bright was indeed a victim, the appearance of Kevin was not expected. Vian&#39;s kids may or may not have been expected. Anna never showed up &#40;though I agree that it was actually the daughter he was after - despite his using &#34;Anna&#34; in the poem two months later&#41;. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think the evidence looks as though he did a great deal of watching. Maybe &#34;scoping out&#34; in advance, but there are lots of ways to do this.  He could be a mailman - or a guy out walking his dog or jogging. <BR> <BR>&#40;I would assume the mailman angle has already been investigated.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2913-->
<!--Post: 2914--><!--Time: 1104268423-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2914"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 1:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think the theories about BTK hiding to watch potential victims implies that everything always went as expected.  How so?  Just because BTK may have watched his victims for a period of time before attacking them in no way insures things would have gone perfectly. <BR> <BR>In the same way, things happening unexpectedly during an attack wouldn&#39;t mean that BTK didn&#39;t bother to hide and watch, either.  However you look at it, we don&#39;t know what BTK did or didn&#39;t do in preparation of a murder. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve often thought that there were probably a lot more potential victims than there were actual victims.  Some people have very busy households all day long.  Reltatives, friends and neighbors stop by throughout the day.  People like that probably would have been crossed off of BTK&#39;s list fairly quickly if he bothered to observe them.  There would have been too many surprises in store for him. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think BTK wanted any surprises.  I think he&#39;s a control freak and that&#39;s why I tend to believe he spent time watching his intended victims.  He wanted absolute control and he didn&#39;t want to get caught, but he&#39;s only human and, like the rest of us, what he wants and what he gets can be two different things.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2914-->
<!--Post: 2918--><!--Time: 1104274361-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2918"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 2:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How about BTK being a bus driver? Public transportation bus driver with Tuesdays and Thursdays off. Or a regular bus passenger? <BR>Are any or all of the murder scenes within sight of a bus route or bus stop?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2918-->
<!--Post: 2922--><!--Time: 1104280155-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2922"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 4:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Being a bus driver/bus passenger would certainly be a way for him to notice people, even if they weren&#39;t people on his bus.  Parking his car a few miles away, then taking a bus to arrive closer to the crime scene &#40;&amp; leaving the same way&#41; could be possible, too.  That way, if anyone happened to notice his vehicle where he&#39;d parked it, it wouldn&#39;t be close enough to the crime scene to seem relevant. <BR> <BR>I think BTK would be excited to ride on a bus with people, knowing he was going to commit murder.  Afterwards, that would probably be even more exciting to him. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know anything about the bus routes that may have been in the area.  Anyone know? <BR> <BR>I definitely believe he had Tuesdays and Thursdays off.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2922-->
<!--Post: 2941--><!--Time: 1104301056-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2941"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 28, 2004 - 10:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Perhaps he wasn&#39;t hiding at all. <BR> <BR>Remember, as satan was God&#39;s most beautiful angel at one time this monster most likely was/is a &#34;normal&#34; looking person and not a boogey man. <BR> <BR>That in and of itself is frightful but he and it, like Satan,  will end one day and that is for sure. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2941-->
<!--Post: 2954--><!--Time: 1104330346-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2954"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->We would all be horrified if we knew the full extent of available surveillance equipment. I supervised an intern in 1976 who had worked for a surveillance equipment co. She stated that they were demonstrating their wares to potential buyers. They were on an upper floor and homed in on a couple having sex about 2 miles away. They could read the numbers on the telephone, and called them. Of course, this was being watched on a screen. That was back when the phone numbers were posted on the body of the phone. Needless to say, the couple was much surprised. If that technology was available in 1976, imagine what could be done now. <BR> <BR>There are binoculars as well. I had a camera lens that doubled as a telescope and brought things so close that it was disorienting. BTK could seek a higher floor. take bird pics in the park, etc. <BR> <BR>Q, I like your thinking.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2954-->
<!--Post: 2982--><!--Time: 1104353220-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2982"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryddik<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryddik<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 12:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was thinking how many people pay attention to a man walking his dog? If most of the murders are in an area close to a park he could stay there for hours and throw a dog a ball and no one would take a second look at him. Also wasn&#39;t it said that he showed a picture of a dog and not a woman. It would also explain why someone would open the door for him they would reconize him from his daily &#34;dog walks&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2982-->
<!--Post: 2983--><!--Time: 1104354532-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2983"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 1:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q is right. When BTK is finally known he will be a real disappointment to those who are expecting a drooling, growling monster. BTK will be an average, non-descript person that could look like you or me. The worst evil of all usually comes in the banal, the plain and the innocent looking and sounding.  <BR> <BR>The reason BTK has never been caught is because, just like Satan, he hasn&#39;t been NOTICED &#40;excellent point on that Q !&#41;. He hides in plain site because he is plain and simply plain and simple, at least in his outward appearance and attitude. If you are a Wichitan you have possibly stood in line at the movies next to BTK, or sat near him in church, or done business with him, or maybe even bought him a drink at the local pub. Perhaps you have dated his daughter. Perhaps you have dated HIM. He looks and acts just like one of us, although he is anything but. As BTK said himself, and I am quoting from memory so I might not get this exactly right, &#34;after a thing like Fox I go home and live my life just like you do&#34;. Anyway, words to that effect. BTK almost certainly never left Wichita; at least not for prison or psychiatric hospital. He has effectively hidden in plain sight for 30 years because it is the best camoflauge of all for monsters like him. He doesn&#39;t blend into the scenery, he often IS the scenery. <BR> <BR>BTK will, at the end of the day, be a profound disappointment to anyone looking for a sexy, television ending. He will be just what one expects if one understands that evil triumphs when mediocrity rises, and evil always cloakes itself in the average. BTK will never be noticed, except by his victims and on the day he is finally brought to justice. Even then people will see a plain, simple, boring man instead of the personification of evil that he is.  <BR> <BR>He and Satan are never caught in time, evil is never confronted in time, because they are never noticed in time. We need to start noticing and looking for evil intentionally. BTK is out there today, going to the store, reading the EAGLE, watching TV, preparing his dinner, perhaps reading this post and laughing at all of us talking about him and starting websites to talk about him and focusing on him as nothing has focused on him before. Evil and Satan love thier own glories. He IS Satan, and he is nothing and we never even noticed him at all. By human standards there was probably not much to notice. He has been a nothing his whole life. But one day, we will, and justice will both notice and remember him through the ages. But then again, he is not human. He is something beneath. Only something from hell could torture and murder children and destroy families and the futures of innocents as he has done repeatedly. <BR> <BR>He will be the one who reminds us to seek out evil before it seeks us out, and his victims, and thier voices will remind all of us that never again can evil be left unconfronted and unnoticed for 3 decades without those voices calling out from the heights for something better. For BTK&#39;s victims, and for all the victims of the self agrandizing and absolute evil that BTK not only represents, but is.  <BR> <BR>The &#34;factor X&#34; that BTK blathers on about is not a mystery at all; it is simply evil incarnate in the average mediocrity that is BTK. Evil personified. With a three initial nickname. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2983-->
<!--Post: 2997--><!--Time: 1104361382-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2997"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 3:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dpinva... thanx for the props but I just want to point out that Satan and evil are not from Hell. Hell was created for Satan and his angels to spend Eternity in. <BR> <BR>Satan&#39;s end has been determined but the spiritual isn&#39;t subject to time as we and ultimately BTK is. <BR> <BR>Satan unlike BTK comes as a beautiful stunning frauad disguised as a angel of light... my point was that BTK and He are not what we expect &#40;unless you read the Bible&#41; or what our fears and Hollywood build them up to be. <BR> <BR>BTK certainly does blend in but someone close enough would surely see a oddnesss that if thought thru would lead them to this murderers crimes... problem is he may not be close to anyone.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2997-->
<!--Post: 3010--><!--Time: 1104370850-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3010"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I always wondered if Btk was a  Postman. Does anybody ever keep an eye on the mailman? Would any of the murder locations be on the same route? I think they are close enough to be. Who would be alarmed if the mailman knocked on your door?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3010-->
<!--Post: 3022--><!--Time: 1104374794-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3022"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wouldnt the mailman look out of place at your door before 7am? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3022-->
<!--Post: 3032--><!--Time: 1104376389-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3032"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Was there a morning paper in Wichita during that era?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3032-->
<!--Post: 3033--><!--Time: 1104376405-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3033"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think anyone who should be passing by fairly quickly would look out of place if they lingered too long. <BR> <BR>A man walking their dog, for instance, would need to be moving along.  I don&#39;t see how BTK could get any valuable information about the activity at a potential victim&#39;s home by just walking by with a dog or if he was jogging or strolling by or going by as a mailman.  The thing all these activities have in common are that these people aren&#39;t stationary.  A person would need to be able to stay still in order to see what was going on at someone&#39;s house. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3033-->
<!--Post: 3037--><!--Time: 1104378334-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3037"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well Jujuree you have just given ME an idea.  You said that all these people arent stationary. <BR>Your right!!  What about this?  We know that he parked The Oteros car at a Dillons grocery and to my best understanding, these were common in Wichita.  Do you remember the old days when mom used to have the grocery clerk bring her groceries to the house?  She would invite him in and he would bring the packages into the kitchen and await his two bits or something like that.  Plenty of time to scope the scene; not out of place; invitation inside.  you tell me!!! <BR> <BR>Lets for a moment go back to Dillons.  Possibly this was a familiar place to him.  Thats why he dumped the car there.  He wouldnt appear out of place there either.  Maybe with their car he would but is that something anyone would have paid attention to?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3037-->
<!--Post: 3040--><!--Time: 1104378944-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3040"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 7:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->VDUBGUY- the title of the thread was watching w/out being watched. A mailman could gather info 5 days a week. Going up and down both sides of the street. Even knock on your door without being suspicous. Not that he would be there at 7AM or commit a murder while carrying his route. But he could use his info on his day off or at night. Its not far fetched, many postal workers are miltary vets. They also have a good deal of knowledge of people in their neighborhood.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3040-->
<!--Post: 3049--><!--Time: 1104381718-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3049"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think BTK would have commited murder in a neighborhood where he could be recognized.  If he&#39;s a mailman, I don&#39;t think he would have killed in the neighborhood where he works.  Maybe in a neighborhood where he worked once in a great while to fill in for somebody, but not where people would know him as their regular mail carrier. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know my mailman&#39;s name, or anything personal about him, but I know what he looks like.  If I saw him out of uniform in a different environment, it might take me a moment, but I&#39;d figure out that was my mailman.  I can&#39;t imagine BTK would risk somebody looking out their window one day and seeing him entering or leaving a victim&#39;s home. <BR> <BR>I believe that other than actually entering the home to kill, then exiting afterwards, BTK took no other chances of being seen in any sort of suspicious way &#40;or at all&#41;.  This is a guy who does not want to get caught.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3049-->
<!--Post: 3054--><!--Time: 1104387651-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3054"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 10:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well a neighborhood can be a very busy place full of people who are not out of place at any given time year-round. Which one is BTK? <BR> There goes a bus with the same driver who passes everyday and in their bus are many passengers who use it everyday and look out the same windows at the same scenery. Several different cab companies have taxies that are picking up or dropping off fares or passing through to or from some place else. <BR>There in the street is somebody working on a sewerpipe or waterline while up above is the phone company working on a line and the next pole down the street has an electrician working on a transformer. Over there the cable televison provider is expanding their coverage area and are laying lines. <BR>Recent wind storms have damaged trees lining the streets and sidewalks so the city has sent out triming crews. The city has also sent out an asphalt crew to fix those reoccuring potholes in the street. Meanwhile the neighbors gardner is busy at work in their yard while the nieghbor across the way is redoing their entire lawn and has hired a landscaper. The older couple up the street has that guy that comes around to help them out in the summer by mowing their lawn and in the winter by shoveling their snow. <BR>Speaking of snow there goes a city truck speading sand or salt on that icy intersection.  <BR>The neighborhood used to have a local kid on his bicycle tossing the paper on the lawn but he was replaced by a guy in car who tosses the rolled paper from his window onto your driveway before the sun comes up. Here comes the mailman and it&#39;s the third guy who&#39;s been assigned this route in less than a year. <BR>Time for insurance policy renewals and the agent comes to your home. On the other side of the street is a guy selling encylopedia&#39;s door to door. Here comes a guy with bible tracts out witnessing for the Jehovah&#39;s, or so he claims and there goes two young men in white shirts and ties walking down the sidewalk doing their mandatory two year missionary work for the Morman&#39;s, or so they say. A man is out walking his dog. I guess he lives around here because I think I&#39;ve seen him before. And there is a jogger on his way to the park. <BR>The realtor is showing a house to a propective buyer. The guy with the rental property is giving a potential rentor a walk through. Both had their properties repaired recently and had housepainters inside and out. Painters were on scaffolds outdoors doing the trim and scraping off paint for a couple weeks. One of the places needed roofing done and they had guys on the roof tearing up shingles and laying down new ones. <BR>A police cruiser working their district passes by slowly.  <BR>A couple of streets down you&#39;ve got that astronomy buff. At least he says he&#39;s looking at the stars. <BR>The telephone repair van passes followed by the truck delivering the new sofa from the furniture store and behind him is a television repair van from the radio and TV store and behind him is a truck from the appliance store delivering a new stove.   <BR>Here comes that police cruiser again. <BR>No officer, I haven&#39;t seen anyone out of the ordinary.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3054-->
<!--Post: 3062--><!--Time: 1104401958-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3062"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 2:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A very good picture of neighborhood activity, Johno! <BR> <BR>I do believe BTK may have picked out victims of interest this way if he didn&#39;t already know them.  As he was going about his own daily activity/work, he may have spied someone he wanted to kill &#40;however a person meets that criteria for him&#41;, but I don&#39;t think he watched them this way. <BR> <BR>You can&#39;t watch someone&#39;s house while you&#39;re driving by on a bus.  You can spot them in their yard and come back later, but you&#39;ve got to be someplace where no one sees you watching. <BR> <BR>Now, something like roofing a house, as you mentioned, could be possible.  A roofer is pretty much in the same place as he&#39;s putting shingles on and the job could take a few days, depending on the amount of work being done.  The astronomy buff?  Definitely a possibility, but if he lives in the neighborhood, he could be easily recognized coming or going from a victim&#39;s home.  Even the new mailman can&#39;t just hang around.  He might pick out a victim, but he also has to come back later to watch that victim. <BR> <BR>The reason why I&#39;m so into this &#34;watching&#34; thing is that I don&#39;t believe BTK wanted to take any unnecessary chances on getting caught.  Obviously, that didn&#39;t always seem to work out for him, but I think he was a planner.  He wanted to have as much time as possible with his victims, so he had to find the optimum time to kill them. <BR> <BR>This is why I don&#39;t believe he did his observing in the dark.  All his killing wasn&#39;t in the dark.  What good would it do, planning-wise, to creep around someone&#39;s house at midnight if you were going to kill during the afternoon? <BR> <BR>Assuming BTK was employed or had some sort of life where he had to be certain places at certain times &#40;like a college student even&#41;, he had time constraints.  For BTK, there were probably only certain days he was available to kill.  Since all but one attack &#40;if I&#39;m remembering correctly&#41; happened on Tuesdays and Thursdays, that makes me think he was available on those days. <BR> <BR>I also believe &#34;the hunt&#34; was part of what he enjoyed.  I think he would have liked to have watched the person he was going to kill, maybe stretching that experience out for several weeks.  When I say several weeks, I don&#39;t mean everyday.  I mean on Tuesdays and Thursdays, during certain times. <BR> <BR>He could establish what those &#34;certain times&#34; were pretty quickly.  For example, I&#39;ll play BTK for a sec here: <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve picked out a woman I want to kill &#40;however that&#39;s done&#41;.  I know where she lives and I have Tuesdays and Thursdays off from my job.  She&#39;s married and has kids.  I only want to deal with her.  The husband leaves for work at 7:30 in the morning, then the kids leave at 7:45.  None of them return for lunch.  The kids get home at 3:00 and the husband returns from work at 5:30. <BR> <BR>From watching for one day, I know I will not be entering the home before 7:45 and I must be finished before 3:00.  A variation on this could be if the mother leaves to take her children to school at 7:45 and returns at 8:00, I could then plan to break in while she&#39;s gone and be waiting for her when she returns, otherwise I know I must enter the home while she is there, probably by just knocking, then forcing my way in.  Depending on what other activity I observe, I now know I could be lucky enough to be with her from about 8:00 to 3:00 if I choose to. <BR> <BR>So, based on that one day of observation, I know I can narrow my watching times down to 7:45 to 3:00.  Does she go to the store on Tuesdays or Thursdays?  Does she have a class she attends on either of those days?  Do people come to visit her?  If so, do they mainly do that in the morning or the afternoon?  Does she have a part time job? <BR> <BR>If I was wanting to kill, savor the moment and not be interrupted, I&#39;d damn sure want to know that her sister &#40;who happens to have a key&#41; doesn&#39;t come buy every day at random times with her two toddlers and a Grandma in tow. <BR> <BR>So, for whatever reason I picked that woman out as a potential victim, she would also have to meet another criteria for me to follow through with killing her.  She would have to live a life that gave me the opportunity to follow through without getting caught.  If her husband also has Tuesdays and Thursdays off, then I wouldn&#39;t bother with her unless I decided to kill him, too. <BR> <BR>This is the sort of thing I think BTK did if he did indeed watch people and I think he really enjoyed this part of it.  I think the &#34;watching&#34; was the foreplay. <BR> <BR>Of course I don&#39;t know anymore than anyone else &#40;except BTK&#41;, so for all I know he might have just followed women home from some place where he saw them for the first time without caring who else might be around and killed them right then.  Or he may have just followed them to see where they lived, then pretty much came right back on his first Tuesday or Thursday off and killed them.  He may have had such an ego that he didn&#39;t believe anyone could stop him anyway.  If ten  people dropped by while he was killing, his plan may have been to kill all ten people. <BR> <BR>I hope all that made sense.  I&#39;ve stayed up way too late! <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3062-->
<!--Post: 3069--><!--Time: 1104419990-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3069"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Murco<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Murco<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 7:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->right on jujuree! <BR>organized sk&#39;s tend to have a lot of miles on their cars, from trolling around looking for victims at random. he would definitely be driving by and checking up on them. his car would be neat and clean, be properly maintained, and probably have a police scanner in it. not to mention his kit.  <BR>someone close to him has had to have seen his kit! <BR>it&#39;s likely he did his own stakeouts, but i think he just &#34;cruised&#34; by often. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3069-->
<!--Post: 3122--><!--Time: 1104469989-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3122"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 9:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If he was a &#34;mailman&#34; why would he need to knock on the back door of the post office to deliver a letter to be put in the TV stations box... at 4:00am in the summer... wearing gloves? <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/1/80.html?1104380131" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/1/80.html? 1104380131</a> <BR> <BR>Of course he might have not been employed any longer by the USPS though but he might have been familiar with the 4:00am shift and that is why he chose the back door then... risk of being recognised??? Hiding in plain site? <BR> <BR>If someone else mentioned this... sorry i didn&#39;t have time to read all the longer posts yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3122-->
<!--Post: 3135--><!--Time: 1104479409-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3135"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 11:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good point Q. By listing some possibilities and eliminating them to the best of our logic we can at least look at who BTK may have been in his everyday life and who he probably wasn&#39;t. If indeed he could have blended in, kept watch descretely, noted times when someone would be home alone, etc.  <BR>In my neighborhood sceanario I left out a couple of other people who make the rounds regulary. The Garbage collectors and the meter reader.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3135-->
<!--Post: 3138--><!--Time: 1104484931-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3138"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 1:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good point about the post office, Q. <BR> <BR>Something else I thought about was people who take surveys.  What if BTK took surveys?  He could either have done surveys for real or just pretended to.  Being a survey taker would be a good part time job for a college student.  Back in the 70&#39;s, it wouldn&#39;t have been unusual for someone to still be going door to door doing something like that. <BR> <BR>Also, if it was a &#34;household&#34; survey of some kind, BTK could have asked all kinds of questions about who was in the home, where do you shop, when do you shop, etc.  Posing as a census taker would be good for that, too, but he would have risked meeting up with someone who knew there was no census being taken at that time. <BR> <BR>He could also have just called on the phone to take the survey. <BR> <BR>While it&#39;s probably unlikely he did anything like that, I was trying to think of a situation where someone might willingly tell a stranger a lot of information about themselves, without being suspicious of the stranger they&#39;re telling it to.  Participating in a survey was the best scenario I came up with.  After all, if BTK could get a potential victim to just tell him what their schedule/habits are, that sure would save him some trouble! <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3138-->
<!--Post: 3143--><!--Time: 1104506347-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3143"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 7:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Didn&#39;t BTK already claim &amp; show multiple fake IDs and refer to them in his letters/puzzles? <BR> <BR>Badge &amp; telephone Co. ? <BR> <BR>The phone Co. fits for being seen but not really noticed but after the fact I think some one would recall it. Mr. Otereo was expecting a phone repair according to his son Charlie, I think. <BR> <BR>A meter reader? <BR> <BR>I think he may have used the cover of darkness to watch and that he knew the victims beforehand from somewhere, <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3143-->
<!--Post: 3157--><!--Time: 1104530466-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3157"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 2:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe btk is very familer with that area of wichita. I would think he grew up there and still lives in the area. I think it is safe to say that btk is claiming he used fake id to gain access to his victims house on at least one occasion. He may have worn some kind of work outfit on this occasion. I do believe some of his victims where stalked by him before their murder. I believe some might not have been. The vian murder I believe was an almost spur of the moment type thing. Watching victims however is his M.O. I believe. I think vian may have been a last second replacement for an other intended victim. I think peeping and stalking btk has been doing all his life. It would be very hard for him to stop this portion of his M.O. He could use tape recordings or other memento&#39;s taken from past victims to substitue for new killings. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3157-->
<!--Post: 3169--><!--Time: 1104538968-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3169"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 4:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dont give up the mailman theory so easily. BTK wanted to get the letter to the box of the post office that rented to KAKE &#40;wichita had more than one post office even in the 70&#39;s&#41;. He obviously didnt work there. And he simply didnt want to just drop it in the mail. &#40;i personally dont think it was BTK that dropped off the letter&#41; But Back to the title of this thread &#34;watch with out being watched.&#34; A mailman that walks his route has ample time to case his victim and never once bring suspicion.  He may have bidded off the route before he chose to fulfill his plan. Its not that far fetched. Try to think of other clues that might fit a mailman. Several other professionals would appear out of place or be easily remembered. This isnt the right place but the baby picture looks a lot like a former carrier from wichita that was my boss once.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3169-->
<!--Post: 3171--><!--Time: 1104540670-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3171"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 4:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Would not be the first time a famous serial killer suspect worked for the post office. Rememeber Son of Sam. But I would be shocked if that where the case. But I would not rule out that Btk is a well known resident in the area where he lives and is well thought of.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3171-->
<!--Post: 3213--><!--Time: 1104621601-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3213"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 3:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->When i was in college i did deliverys for a local delivery company...we could park ANYWHERE, drive almost anywhere, and we would alot of the time use the back door, usually at businesses though. At residences we always went to the front door. Its possible that he may have been a delivery driver, not necessarily a usps employee, they are usually in a hurry to finish a route. Delivery/courier drivers can mill around for even a few minutes unnoticed. Just my 2 cents worth.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3213-->
<!--Post: 3293--><!--Time: 1104752588-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3293"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 3:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In his first letter, BTK wrote &#34;It a big compicated game my friend of the monster play putting victims number down, follow them, checking up on them waiting in the dark,...&#34; &#40; <a href="http://www.christianityoasis.com/PurityPublications/5003/BTK/Home.htm" target=_top>http://www.christianityoasis.com/PurityPublication s/5003/BTK/Home.htm</a> &#41; <BR> <BR>What if this is a clue as to how he selects his victims?  Meter readers &#40;or electric co. employees&#41; and telephone co. professionals &#40;line repairman?&#41; come to mind as types that &#34;put down numbers&#34; of people as part of their work, and would totally &#34;blend in&#34; or be &#34;invisible&#34; as we&#39;re discussing in this thread &#40;and in parallel in another&#41;.  In different ways, both professions might provide time and opportunity for &#34;scoping out&#34; or &#34;casing&#34; victims&#39; homes as well. <BR> <BR>Where I live &#40;in California&#41;, it is not unusual at all for the electric company meter readers to enter our back yards to read our meters in the very early dark of morning.  Also, on a couple of occasions I&#39;ve had disputes with the electric company over usage and the customer service people have told me that the reader must not have been able to &#34;scope&#34; the meter, and estimated my usage instead of getting a precise read.  That is to say: meter readers around here carry telescopes/binoculars.  I have owned a home and worked from my home office for four years, and can only remember seeing my meter reader on two occasions.  Are these things also true in Wichita? <BR> <BR>At this site: <a href="http://www.thoughtpeach.com/archives/000411.html" target=_top>http://www.thoughtpeach.com/archives/000411.html</a>, a commenter calling himself &#34;DWD&#34; says his dad was the man waiting for the payphone while BTK was using it to call WPD, and that his dad said BTK wore a uniform similar to what &#34;a KG&amp;E employee might wear&#34;.  I assume KG&amp;E is the Wichita electric company.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3293-->
<!--Post: 3302--><!--Time: 1104769648-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3302"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 8:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Also, <a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/archive/8348962.htm" target="_blank">here is an excellent summary of the case</a> which I haven&#39;t seen a link posted to elsewhere on catchbtk.com.  It provides lots of details I hadn&#39;t seen reported elsewhere, many regarding issues being &#34;theorized&#34; about in this message board. It confirms the firefighter eyewitness of the BTK payphone call, and his description of BTK as wearing a &#34;grey industrial uniform&#34;, and adds that he was driving a panel van, possibly with writing on the side.  This is precisely the kind of vehicle utility workers around here drive- how about in Wichita?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3302-->
<!--Post: 3580--><!--Time: 1105044016-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3580"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 12:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jujuree <BR> <BR>Well, I don’t think BTK needed to necessarily sit stationary &#40;or even stay very close to the house&#41; in order to watch.  <BR> <BR>If he knew the type of car the Otero’s owned, and he knew where they worked, he could simply place himself strategically along the path of either of their routes and wait for either of them to pass by.  Or perhaps even wait for either them to arrive at work. <BR> <BR>Finding this information was probably easy:   <BR> <BR>The car was probably parked out in their driveway in plain view &#40;or was it?&#41; <BR> <BR>He could have easily followed either of them to check out their routine.  &#40;Again he didn’t need to sit stationary, he could have parked a few streets away &#40;or even park at a fast food parking lot and eat breakfast&#41; and wait for their car to pass him by.&#41;   I think most of us go to work the same route each day, and I am presuming they had a definite routine. <BR> <BR>Also, weren’t the murders early in the morning?   Think about it, how often do you have visitors &#40;or outsiders&#41; that early in the morning at your house?  Most folks are scrambling to get ready &#40;or get the kids ready&#41; for the day. <BR> <BR>So once the car left the premises, I think he thought it was safe to attack.  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3580-->
<!--Post: 3592--><!--Time: 1105050816-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3592"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 2:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Iceateajan, good points. <BR> <BR>I figure if BTK was employed, then his time to be available to attack someone was limited.  He would need to know when the best time would be. He attacked in the afternoon and evening, too.  Some of his attacks he broke in and waited for the victim to get home and in others he entered the home when the victim was already there.  He could be somewhat random about it.  Maybe the possibility of getting caught is a thrill to him, too?  I don&#39;t know.  He just seems like to much of a planner to do anything randomly or to take any unnecessary chances. <BR> <BR>As far as following victims to check out their routines, I think that&#39;s a good possibility.  Especially if he had a point to start at other than their homes, like if he knew where someone worked.  He could always begin following them from their jobs as opposed to following them from their homes.  Good point. <BR> <BR>When it comes to parking a few streets away, I don&#39;t know how someone could do that unless the area is extremely busy, like a business area.  If you&#39;re sitting on a residential street in a car, never getting out, people are going to notice eventually.  Of course, more often than not, a lot of serial killers seem to escape capture for so long because of people not paying attention to their surroundings, thus no witnesses. <BR> <BR>Also, I can&#39;t explain why, but I think BTK just liked to watch his victims.  Not necessarily just for the purposes of attacking them &#40;to get info&#41;, but just to do it and relish in the idea that he knows what he&#39;s going to do to them and they don&#39;t have a clue.  I can easily imagine him following a potential victim to the grocery store.  He might even follow them in, get a cart of his own and pass by them several times in the aisles, getting a little thrill knowing he plans to kill them.  Stuff like that. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3592-->
<!--Post: 3623--><!--Time: 1105070298-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3623"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 7:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jujuree <BR> <BR>&#40;&#40;When it comes to parking a few streets away, I don&#39;t know how someone could do that unless the area is extremely busy, like a business area. If you&#39;re sitting on a residential street in a car, never getting out, people are going to notice eventually.&#41;&#41; <BR> <BR>Yes, but he might have been parked for a only few minutes?  If he knew the approximate time they left or had to arrive at work, then it is possible he could have just needed to sit there for 10 minutes or so. <BR> <BR>Also, if you were to sit on a one-way street, your head could blend in with the head rest, and folks driving by would almost have look back over their shoulder as they pass in order to see someone in the car. <BR> <BR>&#40;&#40;Also, I can&#39;t explain why, but I think BTK just liked to watch his victims.  &#41;&#41; <BR> <BR>Yes, I have that gut feeling also.   <BR> <BR>And speaking of thrill-seeking.  Didn’t he take a chance shooting someone?  Didn’t he think someone might hear it?  Didn’t he also get in the Otero’s car and ride away?  Didn’t he think perhaps a neighbor &#40;who may have been putting out the garbage&#41; would see him drive away? <BR> <BR>Thrill seeking – did anybody ever think his job is/was something dangerous?  Like perhaps climbing dangerous tree limbs in order to cut them down; or perhaps even doing repairs on chimneys, or window washing high buildings, etc.   <BR> <BR>Also, BTK can NOT get away so easy with another killing.  People have cell phones now, people have surveillance cameras the size of a quarter.  You can unwittingly go through a traffic cam, purchase something with a debit card, stop at a convenience store that videocams your visit – electronically you are being tracked.   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3623-->
<!--Post: 3646--><!--Time: 1105080461-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3646"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 10:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You make some very good points.  I never even considered the one-way street thing, but you&#39;re right. <BR> <BR>That thrill seeking part is a good question.  I wouldn&#39;t be surprised if he doesn&#39;t do something for &#34;thrills&#34; like that.  It wouldn&#39;t even have to be a line of work, maybe something he does in his spare time.  He might have been the type to be the first to try bungee jumping when that first became popular, for instance. <BR> <BR>&#40;I think the &#34;thrill seeker&#34; aspect of his personality is worthy of a thread of it&#39;s own, if there isn&#39;t one already.  Maybe the idea could jog the memories/awareness of anyone who may know him?&#41; <BR> <BR>It&#39;s hard to think like a serial killer when you&#39;re not one, LOL.  I can&#39;t help but keep thinking about how I would do this stuff and I&#39;m a big wuss, so that probably doesn&#39;t help me theorize much!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3646-->
<!--Post: 3880--><!--Time: 1105380649-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3880"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Luvmysteries<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Luvmysteries<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 10:10 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Armchairpi, <BR> <BR>I just visited the website <a href="http://www.christianityoasis.com/PurityPublication" target=_top>http://www.christianityoasis.com/PurityPublication</a> s/5003/BTK/Home.htm. Thanks for the link. I read somewhere else on this message board that it is believed that the 911 recording isn&#39;t the entire telephone call. I found it interesting the website you provided that, &#34;The police said they were reasonable certain that the man who called to report the homicide was the same man who killed Fox.. &#34;He knew too many things about her.&#34;&#34; <BR> <BR>I also find it interesting that he has evidently brought two murder weapons with him - a knife and a gun. Has any information been released from the autopsy reports as to the type of knife used? I am relatively new to this message board and I am trying to come up to speed quickly. What kind of gun was used? Was it a rifle? If so, how hard is to to hide in plain sight carryine one? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
